Z||000000||BBBAD GT||07-05-2000||03:40 PM||||I'm curious how fast everybody's Fiero is.  Quarter mile times are perfered, but any 1/8 mi or Gtech 0-60 or such are welcome also.  If your Fiero's weight is significantly different from normal, please list that also.<P>Just for the record, my bone-stock 87 GT went 10.5 in the 1/8 only time out, which is approx low 16's in the quarter.  About average I'd say.  <P>------------------<BR>87 GT, Stock for now<BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT's Web Site</A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||My7Fieros||07-05-2000||04:20 PM||||Fast enough to give a Rustang five point slow a good run for the money!||||reg||12
Z||000002||Taijiguy||07-05-2000||04:57 PM||||LOL  he said 5 point slow...hahahahahahahahaha!!!!!!!<P>DOn't know offhand yet, but soon as I get my carburetor situation worked out I'll be running mine to the Center for Automotive Research at Ohio State University to use their dyno. Should be interesting:<P>.040 2.8 V6<BR>.443 lift @288 deg duration intake<BR>.465 lift @298 deg duration exhaust<BR>Edelbrock 4bbl intake<BR>Either Holley 390 4bbl carb OR<BR>2 Holley/Weber 5200 series carbs (270 cfm per)<BR>Ported/polished<BR>Stock exhaust-restrictions removed<BR>Soon to be custom 2" true dual exh. w/ crossover pipe<BR>No cat<P>Can't wait to see what it'll do. Hope to add a blower or nitrous eventually.<P>Bwahahahahaa! It's ALIVE!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dan86gt3.8||07-05-2000||06:01 PM||||With a pretty well educated guess I would go 1320 feet in about 14.5-15.0 seconds.  Has not ben proven yet...... but maybe around say july 21'st I can let yall know! ||||reg||1
