Z||000009||BBBAD GT||07-06-2000||04:28 PM||||0-60 on a Dyno?  Thats great, but doesn't make it too comparable.  Not everyone does their 0-60 on a dyno.  Traction plays an important part, as does the 1/4 mile.  But, with the 1/4 mi, you have mph speed to sorta see where your HP is at. <P>My7Fieros: so how fast is 'a good run for the money'?  You race Mustangs for money?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>87 GT, Stock for now<BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT's Web Site</A>||||reg||1
Z||000010||My7Fieros||07-07-2000||02:10 AM||||BBAD GT, nope, dont race for money...Im a cop, shouldnt be racing at all....hmmm..<BR>My roommate has a 98 Mustang GT convt....roll bar, SSR Integral wheels, nice ride...Im just not a Mustang fan, waaayyy too many of them out there..a dime a dozen.<BR>Anyway, weve gone at it before, and needless to say, he won..but I did hang with him for a good while though, much better than I thougt it would be.||||reg||1
