Z||000015||Shaun41178||07-08-2000||05:00 PM||||Well I don't think that was the answers he was looking for.  I find it kind of funny how everyone wants to make all these mods to their engines or suspension but not really know how fast it is or how better it can corner.  IT seems many people here want power and when they get it dont' want to know how fast or slow it really is.  Its kind of upsetting really.  Damn people go buy a G-tech or go to a dragstrip and find out!!  some are more then willing to shell out $1500 for a 3.4 and such and then when they get done don't care how fast it will go.  its only $10 to go to a dragstrip and find out or just get a G-tech for $130 and play with it all the time.  Thats what I did.<P>So as far as 0-60 for my car goes its a best of 5.6 and that was a the dragstrip.  Qtr mile checked in at a best of 14.1 at 90 mph.  this was with my 2.8 and not my 3.2 as in my sig  I have yet to get my 3.2 in but it is close so I just put it in my sig.  When my 3.2 goes in I expect high 12's to low 13's in the Qtr and 0-60 of high 4's to low 5's.  All this with an auto tranny too.  <P>------------------<BR>Shaun-Toledo OH, 85 GT<BR>3.2 With nitrous<BR>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178||||reg||1
Z||000016||RobertVol||07-08-2000||05:16 PM||||My stock 88gt runs similar than everybody else with a manny tranny...I have only an underdrive pulley on it thats it. I got a 7.9 0-60 best. 1/4 15.6<P>My 3.8 SC 88GT with some mods <BR>6.2 0-60 best. 1/4 14.5<P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT Top 3.8 SC t top <BR>88GT T top 55k for sale<BR> <A HREF="http://ourworld-top.cs.com/NorthFLFieroClub" TARGET=_blank>http://ourworld-top.cs.com/NorthFLFieroClub</A> <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://ourworld.cs.com/_ht_a/NorthFLFieroClub/1e1ab750.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||GT Bastard||07-08-2000||05:38 PM||||Shaun, I admire the fact that you're so serious about your cars performance, but that doesn't give you the right to dog every one else because they aren't quite "hard-core" enough to live up to your standards.  Just about everytime you post, you go on about how everyone isn't serious about actual performance numbers and how nitrous isn't cheating...  Blah blah blah... The only time you seem to contribute is when you're arguing something.  I'm sure you have lots of information that other forum members could benefit from, but get off your high horse once in a while.   <P>------------------<BR>Gold 86 SE V6 4-sp w/4.10 gears, Eibach springs, Koni's all around w/some poly bushings<BR>Yoko's<BR>Coated headers<BR>ACT 4-puck clutch<BR>MSD ignition<BR>Flowmaster w/ mandrel bent 2.5 pipe<BR>extrude honed intake<BR>Lots of fuel system mods... etc etc...||||reg||1
