Z||000025||Robert||07-10-2000||04:17 PM||||So I’m coming home from West Fest 2000, and I find myself all alone on Interstate 5, on a newly repaved section of the road.   I’m cruising along at 75 and think, what the heck, I’ve never had my car above 90, lets see what “Thunder” will do.  I roll up the windows, drop down the sunroof, put the peddle to the metal.  Within a few seconds I’m doing 110 and the sunroof is being sucked open (should have latched it).  It was still pulling at 115 when I shut it down, I was still 200 miles from my home, and didn’t want to use up all my luck.  Judging by the tack and the amount of pull still left when I shut it down, I think my car will do 125+.<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://canterburytrails.com/photo/fierosig.GIF">  <BR>87GT - "Thunder"||||reg||10
